    verification touchedSetDescendsTheWorkspaceRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "36ad9a26-6ddf-4679-8396-391f2b060fc7"; :>> title = "Sprint 741 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-18"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "Written at close-out, before the verifier is dispatched; avoidable issues scanned (issue011), each finding a tracked item or the reason it is not. (1) UNRECORDED_REACH was first written with the idiom current_dir( - which every integration test carries as Command::current_dir(dir), the CHILD's cwd, not a read of ours - and would have disqualified nearly every converted binary from the recorder key, silently keying them on the whole tree: green, and the whole re-run D0481 exists to remove. Caught by reading the converted sources against the marker before the receipt was written, not by a test. Corrected to current_dir() and the near-miss is now a case in two tests (childs_cwd in a_recorder_reaches_the_tree_only_through_the_support_layer; the Command line in the control's synthetic). No new item: the class - a marker string that matches a neighbouring idiom - has its control in the pair the marker's test now carries, and the DoD's closing clause (no row skipped without a matching key, read from the landed receipt) is where a recurrence shows as a count of recorders that is not eighteen. (2) The CLAUDE.md line never CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR/.. in an integration test was written before any test held it - a reminder (D0047), the shape this repo's own rules forbid. Caught in-sprint; the control no_integration_test_reaches_the_tree_past_the_recording_helpers was added in the same working tree before the commit, over the population test_bearing_sources marks always_test. No new item: the sentence and its control land in one commit; a predicate over which CLAUDE.md sentences are prohibitions and what counts as their control has no defensible boundary (D0088), so the class stays with the review pass's Scope question. (3) The integration fixture in touched_tests_run_before_land.rs has no root Cargo.toml, so the graph path is exercised by wsgraph's fixture and real-workspace tests and by the land itself, not by the fixture that names the land. No new item: adding a manifest tree to that fixture is the next slice's (dcSuiteMeasuresTheWorkspace) own DoD material, since the suite's scope and the touched set's would then read one fixture; noted so it is asked for there. (4) The population floor in the control was typed as nineteen and the tree holds eighteen - the test failed on my own count, not on an offender, and the count was corrected from the failure. Non-finding: the floor is a lower bound so the population cannot silently shrink to zero; the exact count is read from the tree by the DoD's grep. (5) The pre-bash hook denied a python heredoc carrying a backslash inside a print (D0309/issue372 class) and the analysis was written as a scratchpad script instead. Non-finding: the control fired as designed. (6) No Decision was recorded this sprint and none was owed: D0481 states the whole change and is accepted. Non-finding, noted because the review gate's Scope pass says why. (7) The first verifier's touched run (780 passed, DISCREPANCIES: NONE) landed all eighteen recorders WITHOUT a reads_key: the readset directory was joined from the . root the ladder was launched with and handed relative to test processes nextest starts in keel-cli/, so every recorder resolved it under the package, the helper (silent by design) wrote nothing, and each row fell back to the tree key - green, and exactly the whole-tree re-run D0481 exists to remove. Found by reading the receipt back against the DoD's last clause (grep reads_key = 0 of 91 rows) before the recorder was dispatched, not by any test; the cause was confirmed by a probe (one recorder under nextest with an absolute dir wrote its .reads file, with a relative dir wrote nothing) before the fix. Corrected at the site the path leaves the process: capture hands readset_env(readset), an absolutized path, and the_readset_directory_reaches_the_test_processes_absolute is the control (D0047); the second run from a . root landed 18 of 18 with reads_key. No new item: the control is in this commit and the DoD's read-back clause now states the count it found; the class - a fact silently degrading to its fallback with no red - is what issue550's own resolver was, and the receipt's per-row reads_key is the surface a reader checks. The issue570 scratch-name control fired on this test's first negative (a fixed temp_dir name) and the case was rewritten over a synthetic absolute path - non-finding, the control fired as designed."; }
